#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un corso IBM gratuito sull'informazione e il calcolo quantistico"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "Analisi"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll analyze Grover's algorithm to understand how it works.\n"
"We'll start with what could be described as a *symbolic* analysis, where we calculate how the Grover operation $G$ acts on certain states, and then we'll tie this symbolic analysis to a *geometric* picture that's helpful for visualizing how the algorithm works.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ora analizzeremo l'algoritmo di Grover per capire come funziona.\n"
"Partiremo da quella che potrebbe essere descritta come un'analisi *simbolica*, in cui calcoliamo come l'operazione di Grover $G$ agisce su certi stati, e poi collegheremo questa analisi simbolica a un'immagine *geometrica* che è utile per visualizzare il funzionamento dell'algoritmo.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Solutions and non-solutions {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"
msgstr "Soluzioni e non-soluzioni {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by defining two sets of strings.\n"
msgstr "Iniziamo definendo due insiemi di stringhe.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set $A_1$ contains all of the solutions to our search problem while $A_0$ contains the strings that aren't solutions (which we can refer to as *non-solutions* when it's convenient).\n"
"These two sets satisfy $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ and $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n,$ which is to say that this is a *bipartition* of $\\Sigma^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"L'insieme $A_1$ contiene tutte le soluzioni al nostro problema di ricerca, mentre $A_0$ contiene le stringhe che non sono soluzioni (che possiamo chiamare *non-soluzioni* quando è conveniente).\n"
"Questi due insiemi soddisfano $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ e $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n,$ il che significa che questa è una *bipartizione* di $\\Sigma^n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we'll define two unit vectors representing uniform superpositions over "
"the sets of solutions and non-solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Definiamo ora due vettori unitari che rappresentano sovrapposizioni uniformi"
" sugli insiemi di soluzioni e non-soluzioni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Formally speaking, each of these vectors is only defined when its corresponding set is nonempty, but hereafter we're going to focus on the case that neither $A_0$ nor $A_1$ is empty.\n"
"The cases that $A_0 = \\varnothing$ and $A_1 = \\varnothing$ are easily handled separately, and we'll do that later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Formalmente, ciascuno di questi vettori è definito solo quando il corrispondente insieme è non vuoto, ma d'ora in poi ci concentreremo sul caso in cui né $A_0$ né $A_1$ sia vuoto.\n"
"I casi in cui $A_0 = \\varnothing$ e $A_1 = \\varnothing$ si trattano facilmente separatamente, e lo faremo più avanti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an aside, the notation being used here is common: any time we have a "
"finite and nonempty set $S,$ we can write $\\vert S\\rangle$ to denote the "
"quantum state vector that's uniform over the elements of $S.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Come nota a margine, la notazione usata qui è comune: ogni volta che abbiamo"
" un insieme finito e non vuoto $S,$ possiamo scrivere $\\vert S\\rangle$ per"
" indicare il vettore di stato quantistico che è uniforme sugli elementi di "
"$S.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's also define $\\vert u \\rangle$ to be a *uniform* quantum state over "
"all $n$-bit strings:\n"
msgstr ""
"Definiamo anche $\\vert u \\rangle$ come lo stato quantistico *uniforme* su "
"tutte le stringhe di $n$ bit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Notice that\n"
msgstr "Nota che\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle,$ "
"so $\\vert u\\rangle$ represents the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ "
"after the initialization in step 1 of Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Abbiamo anche che $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle,$ "
"quindi $\\vert u\\rangle$ rappresenta lo stato del registro $\\mathsf{Q}$ "
"dopo l'inizializzazione nel passo 1 dell'algoritmo di Grover.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that just before the iterations of $G$ happen in step 2, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ is contained in the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ and moreover the coefficients of these vectors are real numbers.\n"
"As we will see, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ will always have these properties — meaning that the state is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — after any number of iterations of the operation $G$ in step 2.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo implica che appena prima che le iterazioni di $G$ avvengano nel passo 2, lo stato di $\\mathsf{Q}$ è contenuto nello spazio vettoriale bidimensionale generato da $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ e i coefficienti di questi vettori sono numeri reali.\n"
"Come vedremo, lo stato di $\\mathsf{Q}$ avrà sempre queste proprietà — ovvero lo stato sarà una combinazione lineare reale di $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — dopo un qualsiasi numero di iterazioni dell'operazione $G$ nel passo 2.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An observation about the Grover operation {#an-observation-about-the-grover-"
"operation}"
msgstr ""
"Un'osservazione sull'operazione di Grover {#an-observation-about-the-grover-"
"operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We'll now turn our attention to the Grover operation\n"
msgstr "Volgiamo ora la nostra attenzione all'operazione di Grover\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "beginning with an interesting observation about it.\n"
msgstr "partendo da un'interessante osservazione su di essa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine for a moment that we replaced the function $f$ by the composition of $f$ with the NOT function — or, in other words, the function we get by flipping the output bit of $f.$\n"
"We'll call this new function $g,$ and we can express it using symbols in a few alternative ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Immagina per un momento di sostituire la funzione $f$ con la composizione di $f$ con la funzione NOT — ovvero la funzione ottenuta invertendo il bit di output di $f.$\n"
"Chiameremo questa nuova funzione $g,$ e possiamo esprimerla simbolicamente in alcuni modi alternativi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ and therefore\n"
msgstr "per ogni stringa $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ e quindi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that if we were to substitute the function $f$ with the function "
"$g,$ Grover's algorithm wouldn't function any differently — because the "
"states we obtain from the algorithm in the two cases are necessarily "
"equivalent up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ciò significa che se sostituissimo la funzione $f$ con la funzione $g,$ "
"l'algoritmo di Grover non funzionerebbe in modo diverso — perché gli stati "
"ottenuti dall'algoritmo nei due casi sono necessariamente equivalenti a meno"
" di una fase globale.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This isn't a problem!\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the algorithm doesn't care which strings are solutions and which are non-solutions — it only needs to be able to *distinguish* solutions and non-solutions to operate correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo non è un problema!\n"
"Intuitivamente, l'algoritmo non si preoccupa di quali stringhe siano soluzioni e quali non lo siano — ha solo bisogno di essere in grado di *distinguere* soluzioni e non-soluzioni per funzionare correttamente.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Action of the Grover operation {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"
msgstr "Azione dell'operazione di Grover {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider the action of $G$ on the quantum state vectors $\\vert "
"A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Consideriamo ora l'azione di $G$ sui vettori di stato quantistici $\\vert "
"A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's observe that the operation $Z_f$ has a very simple action on "
"$\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Prima di tutto, osserviamo che l'operazione $Z_f$ ha un'azione molto "
"semplice su $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"The operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"In secondo luogo, abbiamo l'operazione $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"L'operazione $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ è definita come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"again for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ and a convenient alternative way to"
" express this operation is like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"sempre per ogni stringa $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ e un modo alternativo comodo per "
"esprimere questa operazione è il seguente:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to verify that this expression agrees with the definition of "
"$Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is to evaluate its action on standard basis states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un modo semplice per verificare che questa espressione corrisponda alla "
"definizione di $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ è valutarne l'azione sugli stati della "
"base standard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ can therefore"
" be written like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"L'operazione $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ può quindi "
"essere scritta così:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"using the same notation, $\\vert u \\rangle,$ that we used above for the "
"uniform superposition over all $n$-bit strings.\n"
msgstr ""
"usando la stessa notazione, $\\vert u \\rangle,$ che abbiamo usato sopra per"
" la sovrapposizione uniforme su tutte le stringhe di $n$ bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we have what we need to compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"First let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ora abbiamo tutto il necessario per calcolare l'azione di $G$ su $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"Calcoliamo prima l'azione di $G$ su $\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "And second, let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "E in secondo luogo, calcoliamo l'azione di $G$ su $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In both cases we're using the equation\n"
msgstr "In entrambi i casi utilizziamo l'equazione\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "along with the expressions\n"
msgstr "insieme alle espressioni\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{e}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "that follow.\n"
msgstr "che ne derivano.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In summary, we have\n"
msgstr "In sintesi, abbiamo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we already noted, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ just prior to step 2 is contained in the two-dimensional space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ and we have just established that $G$ maps any vector in this space to another vector in the same space.\n"
"This means that, for the sake of the analysis, we can focus our attention exclusively on this subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Come già osservato, lo stato di $\\mathsf{Q}$ appena prima del passo 2 è contenuto nello spazio bidimensionale generato da $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ e abbiamo appena dimostrato che $G$ mappa qualsiasi vettore in questo spazio in un altro vettore nello stesso spazio.\n"
"Ciò significa che, ai fini dell'analisi, possiamo concentrare la nostra attenzione esclusivamente su questo sottospazio.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To better understand what's happening within this two-dimensional space, "
"let's express the action of $G$ on this space as a matrix,\n"
msgstr ""
"Per capire meglio cosa accade in questo spazio bidimensionale, esprimiamo "
"l'azione di $G$ su questo spazio come una matrice,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"whose first and second rows/columns correspond to $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ respectively.\n"
"So far in this series, we've always connected the rows and columns of matrices with the classical states of a system, but matrices can also be used to describe the actions of linear mappings on different bases like we have here.\n"
msgstr ""
"le cui prime e seconde righe/colonne corrispondono rispettivamente a $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"Finora in questa serie, abbiamo sempre collegato le righe e le colonne delle matrici agli stati classici di un sistema, ma le matrici possono essere usate anche per descrivere le azioni di mappature lineari su basi diverse come nel nostro caso.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While it isn't at all obvious at first glance, the matrix $M$ is what we "
"obtain by *squaring* a simpler-looking matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebbene non sia affatto ovvio a prima vista, la matrice $M$ è ciò che si "
"ottiene *elevando al quadrato* una matrice dall'aspetto più semplice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix\n"
msgstr "La matrice\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a *rotation matrix*, which we can alternatively express as\n"
msgstr ""
"è una *matrice di rotazione*, che possiamo in alternativa esprimere come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "per\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This angle $\\theta$ is going to play a very important role in the analysis "
"that follows, so it's worth stressing its importance here as we see it for "
"the first time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo angolo $\\theta$ avrà un ruolo molto importante nell'analisi che "
"segue, quindi vale la pena sottolinearne l'importanza la prima volta che lo "
"incontriamo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In light of this expression of this matrix, we observe that\n"
msgstr "Alla luce di questa espressione della matrice, osserviamo che\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is because rotating by the angle $\\theta$ two times is equivalent to rotating by the angle $2\\theta.$\n"
"Another way to see this is to make use of the alternative expression\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo perché ruotare di un angolo $\\theta$ due volte equivale a ruotare di un angolo $2\\theta.$\n"
"Un altro modo per vederlo è utilizzare l'espressione alternativa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "together with the *double angle* formulas from trigonometry:\n"
msgstr "insieme alle formule dell'*angolo doppio* della trigonometria:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"In summary, the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ at the start of step 2 is\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"In sintesi, lo stato del registro $\\mathsf{Q}$ all'inizio del passo 2 è\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and the effect of applying $G$ to this state is to rotate it by an angle $2\\theta$ within the space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"So, for example, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"e l'effetto dell'applicazione di $G$ a questo stato è quello di ruotarlo di un angolo $2\\theta$ all'interno dello spazio generato da $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"Così, ad esempio, abbiamo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and in general\n"
msgstr "e in generale\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Immagine geometrica {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's connect the analysis we just went through to a geometric picture.\n"
"The idea is that the operation $G$ is the product of two *reflections*,\n"
"$Z_f$ and $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"And the net effect of performing two reflections is to perform a *rotation*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Colleghiamo ora l'analisi appena svolta a un'immagine geometrica.\n"
"L'idea è che l'operazione $G$ è il prodotto di due *riflessioni*,\n"
"$Z_f$ e $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"E l'effetto netto dell'esecuzione di due riflessioni è quello di eseguire una *rotazione*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's start with $Z_f.$\n"
"As we already observed previously, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Iniziamo con $Z_f.$\n"
"Come abbiamo già osservato in precedenza, abbiamo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Within the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$\n"
"this is a *reflection* about the line parallel to $\\vert A_0\\rangle,$ which we'll call $L_1.$\n"
"Here's a figure illustrating the action of this reflection on a hypothetical unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$\n"
"which we're assuming is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"All'interno dello spazio vettoriale bidimensionale generato da $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$\n"
"questa è una *riflessione* rispetto alla retta parallela a $\\vert A_0\\rangle,$ che chiameremo $L_1.$\n"
"Ecco una figura che illustra l'azione di questa riflessione su un ipotetico vettore unitario $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$\n"
"che assumiamo essere una combinazione lineare reale di $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Una figura che mostra l'azione di una riflessione su un "
"vettore.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes "
"n},$ which we've already seen can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"In secondo luogo abbiamo l'operazione $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} "
"H^{\\otimes n},$ che abbiamo già visto potersi scrivere come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is also a reflection, this time about the line $L_2$ parallel to the vector $\\vert u\\rangle.$\n"
"Here's a figure depicting the action of this reflection on a unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Anche questa è una riflessione, questa volta rispetto alla retta $L_2$ parallela al vettore $\\vert u\\rangle.$\n"
"Ecco una figura che mostra l'azione di questa riflessione su un vettore unitario $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a second reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Una figura che mostra l'azione di una seconda riflessione su un "
"vettore.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we compose these two reflections, we obtain a rotation — by twice the "
"angle between the lines of reflection — as this figure illustrates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando componiamo queste due riflessioni, otteniamo una rotazione — di un "
"angolo doppio rispetto all'angolo tra le rette di riflessione — come "
"illustra questa figura.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of the Grover operation on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Una figura che mostra l'azione dell'operazione di Grover su un "
"vettore.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This explains, in geometric terms, why the effect of the Grover operation is"
" to rotate linear combinations of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert "
"A_1\\rangle$ by an angle of $2\\theta.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo spiega, in termini geometrici, perché l'effetto dell'operazione di "
"Grover è quello di ruotare le combinazioni lineari di $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ e"
" $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ di un angolo $2\\theta.$\n"
